From: <openlearn-plugin-lab-seat audit>
Date: 2026-09-06
Subject: [PATCH] plugin-sdk: stop value-exporting host runtime classes from public dist

Why
---
Plugins run in a self-contained Worker (import(fileUrl) / data: URL) so the SDK
must be inlined into plugin bundles. Today packages/plugin-sdk/index.ts
value-exports 7 host-runtime classes (PluginRuntimeAdapter, ...,
PluginDistributionManager) which internally import express / jszip / pino /
uuid / semver. SDK's dist therefore keeps top-level third-party imports, and the
plugin CLI (cli.mjs onResolve → sdkDist) inlines the whole dependency tree →
~7.4 MB plugin bundles.

Plugins never instantiate these classes; they consume host-injected instances
via DI Tokens (IPluginDistributionManagerToken, ...), which stay type-only.

Impact
------
- plugin dist/index.js: ~7.4 MB → ~100-200 KB
- zero API loss for plugins: all I*Tokens and Token constants remain exported
- host code that needs the concrete classes imports them from
  ../core/plugin-host directly (server/composition already does).

Change
------
packages/plugin-sdk/index.ts

  // ── Unified Foundation Layer (P7 Sprints) ──────────────────────────────
 
  export type {
    IPluginRuntime,
    IUnifiedPluginContext,
    IPluginLifecycleManager,
    IPluginCapabilityGateway,
    IUnifiedExtensionRegistry,
    IPluginDistributionManager,
    CapabilityMetadata,
    ExtensionItemMetadata,
  } from '../core/plugin-host/index.js';
 
- export {
-   PluginRuntimeAdapter,
-   PluginRuntimeComposition,
-   PluginContextAdapter,
-   PluginLifecycleManager,
-   PluginCapabilityGateway,
-   UnifiedExtensionRegistry,
-   PluginDistributionManager,
- } from '../core/plugin-host/index.js';
+ // NOTE: concrete host-runtime classes are intentionally NOT re-exported here.
+ // Plugins run in a self-contained Worker and must not pull express/jszip/pino
+ // trees into their bundles. Consume host instances via the I*Tokens instead.
+ // Host process code should import these from '../core/plugin-host/index.js'.

Then:
  node packages/plugin-sdk/build.mjs   # regenerate dist/

After rebuild, dist/index.js must no longer top-level import express/jszip/pino.
(expect: 34 KB → ~10 KB)

Follow-up cleanup
-----------------
- packages/server/** / composition modules that imported these through the SDK
  package should import from '../core/plugin-host/index.js' instead.
- optional, later: add "@openlearn/plugin-sdk/runtime" subpath export so advanced
  consumers can opt into the ultra-slim surface (proposal docs/sdk-pr/proposal.md).
